**Key idea:** Exactly one value appears three times and the other seven appear once each. You can write this with a **3-hot position mask** (the same technique as the pair problem). A cleaner alternative uses a **value table**: 8 unique values, and each array slot selects one table entry, with entry 0 selected exactly three times.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  V["vals[8] unique: 40, 3, 77, 9, 61, 25, 88, 12"] --> S["sel[10]: count(sel==0)=3, count(sel==k)=1 for k=1..7"]
  S --> A["a[i] = vals[sel[i]]: 3, 40, 77, 40, 9, 61, 40, 25, 88, 12"]
