**Key idea:** Keep a **non-random history** of the last three successful colors. The constraint excludes every color in the history, and `post_randomize` pushes the new color and trims the history to three. So a color can't come back within the next three draws.

| draw | history before | allowed | picked |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | {} | 0..9 | 4 |
| 2 | {4} | not 4 | 7 |
| 3 | {4,7} | not 4,7 | 1 |
| 4 | {4,7,1} | not 4,7,1 | 9 |
| 5 | {7,1,9} | 4 allowed again | 4 |

### Solution
```systemverilog
class color_stream;
  rand int unsigned color;
  int unsigned history[$];
  int unsigned N = 3;                     // window size
  constraint c_color {
    color inside {[0:9]};
    !(color inside {history});            // same as foreach(history[i]) color != history[i]
  }
  function void post_randomize();
    history.push_back(color);
    if (history.size() > N) void'(history.pop_front());
  endfunction
endclass
```

With an enum:
```systemverilog
typedef enum {RED, GREEN, BLUE, YELLOW, BLACK} color_e;
rand color_e c;
color_e hist[$];
constraint c_no_rep { !(c inside {hist}); }
```

