**Key idea:** Gregorian leap year: `(y % 4 == 0) && (y % 100 != 0 || y % 400 == 0)`. Day ranges then depend on the month. Power of 4: choose an exponent `e` in `0..15` and set `value == 1 << (2*e)`. The bit-trick alternative is "nonzero, one-hot, and only even bit positions."

| year | %4 | %100 | %400 | leap? |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 2024 | 0 | 24 | 24 | yes |
| 1900 | 0 | 0 | 300 | no |
| 2000 | 0 | 0 | 0 | yes |
| 2023 | 3 | 23 | 23 | no |

